<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Magnitogorsk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Magnitogorsk is an industrial city in the southern Urals of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, built from 1929 around a huge iron and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> works beside Magnitnaya, the 'magnetic mountain' of iron ore. Constructed at great speed during Stalin's first Five-Year Plan, partly by forced labour, it became a symbol of Soviet industrialisation. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> its works produced a large share of Soviet steel for tanks and shells.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/magnitogorsk.jpg" alt="Magnitogorsk" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hellmaster_ru · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Magnitogorskiy_Gos_Tekh_Universitet.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
